From bee0fdaf6b785d15acc45f5b5b5482b995c52643 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 00:46:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 95/96] hir_conv: const-eval bitreverse shifted the result one
 bit too far

The loop set the low bit and then shifted, so it returned
`reverse(x) << 1` truncated to the type: `1u16.reverse_bits()` was 0,
`0x8003u16` gave 0x8002. Only compile-time evaluation was affected (the
C output uses __mrustc_bitrev*), but crates build lookup tables that way:
miniz_oxide 0.8.9 `static REVERSED_BITS_LOOKUP: [u16; 512]` (every
inflate of dynamic or fixed Huffman blocks fails, "corrupt deflate
stream"; syntect's syntax dumps in deff 0.4.2), and crc 3's tables for
reflected algorithms (e.g. CRC-32) through `poly.reverse_bits()` in
const fns. Shift first, then set the bit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hir_conv/constant_evaluation.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/hir_conv/constant_evaluation.cpp b/src/hir_conv/constant_evaluation.cpp
index e0ec23a6..49dff12e 100644
--- a/src/hir_conv/constant_evaluation.cpp
+++ b/src/hir_conv/constant_evaluation.cpp
@@ -2695,10 +2695,10 @@ namespace HIR {
                     auto val = local_state.read_param_uint(ti.bits, e.args.at(0));
                     U128    rv;
                     for(size_t i = 0; i < ti.bits; i ++) {
+                        rv <<= 1;
                         if( (val & 1) != 0 ) {
                             rv |= 1;
                         }
-                        rv <<= 1;
                         val >>= 1;
                     }
                     dst.write_uint(state, ti.bits, rv);
